Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-23
Subject: Guard symtable's withrefnode free against nil and strpas the messageinf compare
License: expat

Two narrow fixes in `symtable.pas`:

- `twithsymtable.destroy` calls `tobject(withrefnode).free` unconditionally.
  In native FPC `TObject.Free` is null-safe (the method itself short-circuits
  on `Self = nil`), but tp2cc does not model that null-safe-method-on-nil
  contract. Wrap the call with `if assigned(withrefnode) then` so the call
  site never reaches the method on a nil instance.

- The message-method search compares `tprocdef(def).messageinf.str` (a
  `pchar`) directly against `s` (a Pascal string). That equality relies on
  Pascal's implicit `pchar`-to-string conversion, which the bootstrap subset
  does not fold automatically. Wrap with `strpas(...)` so the comparison is
  string-to-string with no implicit conversion involved.

--- a/compiler/symtable.pas
+++ b/compiler/symtable.pas
@@ -1685,7 +1685,8 @@

     destructor twithsymtable.destroy;
       begin
-        tobject(withrefnode).free;
+        if assigned(withrefnode) then
+          tobject(withrefnode).free;
         symsearch:=nil;
         inherited destroy;
       end;
@@ -2035,7 +2036,7 @@
              begin
                if (def.deftype=procdef) and
                   (po_msgstr in tprocdef(def).procoptions) and
-                  (tprocdef(def).messageinf.str=s) then
+                  (strpas(tprocdef(def).messageinf.str)=s) then
                 begin
                   sym:=tprocdef(def).procsym;
                   if assigned(topclassh) then
